WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.755
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:04.025 --> 00:09.025
Don't you think dreams are strange?

3
00:12.385 --> 00:13.945
Sometimes they drift.

4
00:14.505 --> 00:16.184
Sometimes they're a blur.

5
00:17.185 --> 00:19.065
They seem so vivid,

6
00:19.145 --> 00:22.345
but once you wake up, they're gone.

7
00:25.905 --> 00:28.745
This is the story of a little cat,

8
00:28.825 --> 00:33.465
kept in a cage where she wasn't even allowed to dream.

9
00:33.545 --> 00:38.665
Yet, she discovered something more beautiful than anyone else ever had.

10
00:41.145 --> 00:47.425
And perhaps this story might help us answer a question.

11
00:50.185 --> 00:52.985
But what was the question again?

12
01:06.545 --> 01:08.345
We've always believed

13
01:08.425 --> 01:12.825
that a good society needs people with knowledge,

14
01:12.905 --> 01:15.505
moral values, and good manners.

15
01:15.585 --> 01:17.985
That's why we at Saint Cecilia School

16
01:18.065 --> 01:21.345
are committed to nurturing our girls into the finest young ladies.

17
01:21.425 --> 01:23.465
Otherwise, we wouldn't have been ranked

18
01:23.545 --> 01:25.505
in the country's top five for ten years.

19
01:26.265 --> 01:27.385
We have to expand

20
01:27.465 --> 01:29.265
our Hall of Fame every year, you know.

21
01:29.345 --> 01:31.185
As for our top students,

22
01:31.265 --> 01:33.705
I'm proud of every one of them.

23
01:34.825 --> 01:36.785
What's that?

24
01:36.865 --> 01:39.865
Who are this year's top students?

25
01:39.945 --> 01:42.985
Perhaps we shouldn't focus so much on who's on top.

26
01:43.065 --> 01:44.185
Equality, you know.

27
01:44.265 --> 01:45.665
Everyone is equal.

28
01:46.785 --> 01:48.505
The top students in our school?

29
01:48.585 --> 01:49.625
Which category do you mean?

30
01:50.225 --> 01:53.865
Grades, looks, or how rich they are?

31
01:53.945 --> 01:56.025
Well, they've got it all.

32
01:56.105 --> 01:57.705
It's got to be the Toxxxxin girls, right?

33
01:58.505 --> 01:59.865
Make sure you spell it with four X's.

34
01:59.945 --> 02:00.825
There's Aidao.

35
02:00.905 --> 02:01.945
OUTSTANDING STUDENT

36
02:02.025 --> 02:03.585
Gale.

37
02:04.465 --> 02:07.385
Chelsea and Meimei.

38
02:07.465 --> 02:08.985
Four girls, four different styles.

39
02:09.065 --> 02:10.265
But one thing's for sure.

40
02:10.345 --> 02:13.465
They're all gorgeous and rich.

41
02:13.545 --> 02:14.705
They're cool too, you know.

42
02:14.785 --> 02:17.145
They dare to be different and be themselves.

43
02:17.225 --> 02:18.905
And they get good grades too.

44
02:18.985 --> 02:20.425
Who could have a problem with that?

45
02:20.505 --> 02:22.345
So, there was this empty club room

46
02:22.425 --> 02:24.345
at our school, right?

47
02:24.425 --> 02:26.345
Then one day, they just put up a sign

48
02:26.425 --> 02:27.865
and claimed the whole room for themselves.

49
02:27.945 --> 02:29.265
Iconic.

50
02:29.865 --> 02:32.025
Why didn't the school do anything?

51
02:34.905 --> 02:36.745
There have been rumors, you know.

52
02:36.825 --> 02:38.025
They just get away with everything.

53
02:38.105 --> 02:40.945
Good for them. This school is boring as hell.

54
02:41.945 --> 02:43.345
They're total trendsetters.

55
02:43.425 --> 02:45.865
They dare to do what no one else will.

56
02:45.945 --> 02:47.465
Seriously, they're my idols.

57
02:49.425 --> 02:50.265
Yeah.

58
02:50.345 --> 02:52.025
I guess I like how mysterious they are too.

59
02:52.105 --> 02:53.665
All their social media is private.

60
02:55.585 --> 02:57.625
Is that strange? Not really.

61
02:57.705 --> 02:59.745
I guess that's just how the elite are.

62
02:59.825 --> 03:01.065
Especially Aidao.

63
03:01.145 --> 03:02.665
You can barely find anything about her.

64
03:02.745 --> 03:04.065
But then, look at her last name.

65
03:04.145 --> 03:05.385
AIDAO LAOSATHITPHONG

66
03:05.465 --> 03:07.705
If I had her last name,

67
03:08.545 --> 03:09.625
I'd probably do the same.

68
03:09.705 --> 03:11.185
Her family keeps everything under wraps.

69
03:20.785 --> 03:27.745
Hey, now that you're defense minister, I don't think you need to throw a party.

70
03:27.825 --> 03:31.225
Why not save it for when you become prime minister next term?

71
03:31.305 --> 03:32.745
What do you say, Sathit?

72
03:34.985 --> 03:36.865
You're giving me too much credit.

73
03:36.945 --> 03:40.385
But having one on standby wouldn't hurt.

74
03:40.905 --> 03:41.905
Sure.

75
03:43.105 --> 03:45.225
You're quite the powerful family now.

76
03:45.305 --> 03:47.865
Both father and son.

77
03:47.945 --> 03:50.585
So, young man, your name's Din, right?

78
03:50.665 --> 03:51.505
Yes, sir.

79
03:51.585 --> 03:54.265
I hear you're top of your political science class.

80
03:55.705 --> 03:57.785
There aren't many major courses in the first year, sir.

81
03:57.865 --> 04:01.225
You already look promising. Why not introduce him to the public?

82
04:01.305 --> 04:03.785
Absolutely not. You know how it is.

83
04:03.865 --> 04:06.465
These days, people on social media are always ready to attack us.

84
04:07.105 --> 04:10.905
I won't let Din go on social media until he's truly ready.

85
04:11.905 --> 04:15.545
Hey, don't be so strict with him.

86
04:15.625 --> 04:20.184
Still, just don't do anything stupid.

87
04:21.064 --> 04:23.585
I can't be bothered laughing at you.

88
04:45.505 --> 04:49.705
Don't put too much pressure on me.

89
04:50.385 --> 04:51.265
Please.

90
04:52.905 --> 04:54.025
All right, all right.

91
04:54.105 --> 04:57.145
But I really can't help it.

92
04:58.225 --> 05:01.865
There are quite a few black sheep in my family,

93
05:01.945 --> 05:04.225
so I have to be extra careful.

94
05:06.425 --> 05:07.385
Isn't that right, Jes?

95
05:18.705 --> 05:20.705
You never miss a chance to take a dig at me

96
05:21.345 --> 05:23.305
whenever this comes up, do you?

97
05:23.385 --> 05:24.505
Am I wrong, though?

98
05:25.265 --> 05:27.105
Good thing you stopped using our last name.

99
05:27.185 --> 05:29.425
I wouldn't dare cause trouble for the Laosathitphong family.

100
05:30.585 --> 05:34.545
Besides, my new last name is much more stylish.

101
05:35.585 --> 05:36.545
Jessada Wei.

102
05:37.105 --> 05:38.585
Cool, huh?

103
05:44.705 --> 05:46.425
Congratulations, big brother.

104
05:49.905 --> 05:51.305
And congratulations to you too, Din.

105
05:53.265 --> 05:54.985
Especially on your English score.

106
05:55.065 --> 05:58.905
For a subject you struggle with, that score was strangely good, wasn't it?

107
05:59.705 --> 06:02.865
Hey, where are you going, Jes?

108
06:02.945 --> 06:06.945
I'll go enjoy some peace and quiet, like a black sheep should.

109
06:20.145 --> 06:21.385
Toxic.

110
06:22.305 --> 06:23.545
Toxic.

111
06:24.545 --> 06:25.905
Toxic.

112
06:42.785 --> 06:48.665
What kind of high school kid takes exams for a university student like you?

113
06:48.745 --> 06:51.785
You know, you could knock first, Uncle.

114
06:52.625 --> 06:56.145
And that's what we call a fair trade.

115
06:56.225 --> 06:59.385
When my dear brother asks his little sister for help,

116
07:01.905 --> 07:03.825
I have to make him owe me.

117
07:04.505 --> 07:05.665
It might come in handy someday.

118
07:07.105 --> 07:08.825
You're good at making people owe you.

119
07:08.905 --> 07:11.105
Just like you do with me, right?

120
07:11.185 --> 07:12.345
Of course.

121
07:14.625 --> 07:17.105
Here's that Summer Trend questionnaire

122
07:17.185 --> 07:19.705
you asked me to get the younger kids at school to fill out.

123
07:22.705 --> 07:25.145
You're getting better at this every day.

124
07:26.065 --> 07:31.145
I'd rather have your help than your praise.

125
07:32.385 --> 07:34.585
What are you talking about? I have no idea what you mean.

126
07:34.665 --> 07:35.985
What do you want from me?

127
07:36.065 --> 07:38.025
My record collection? Go pick something.

128
07:38.105 --> 07:40.625
Come on, no. I need the usual favor.

129
07:40.705 --> 07:42.225
Keep a lookout for me.

130
07:43.945 --> 07:48.385
The Toxxxxin girls have plans to go wild today.

131
07:51.185 --> 07:52.225
I'm counting on you.

132
07:55.785 --> 07:57.585
These crazy wildcats.

133
08:11.345 --> 08:13.265
Hey! What the hell happened?

134
08:34.305 --> 08:36.664
Do I think the Toxxxxin girls go wild

135
08:36.745 --> 08:39.065
when they're outside school?

136
08:39.784 --> 08:41.425
No way.

137
08:45.505 --> 08:47.465
Their grades are so good.

138
08:47.545 --> 08:50.545
I bet studying alone keeps them busy.

139
08:56.505 --> 08:57.785
Hobbies?

140
09:01.145 --> 09:04.505
I'm sure they have some. But probably something fancy and expensive.

141
09:04.585 --> 09:05.545
I'm kind of curious too.

142
09:05.625 --> 09:07.905
Like, glamorous princess stuff?

143
09:07.985 --> 09:09.785
It must be fabulous.

144
09:44.985 --> 09:47.305
Tonight was fucking amazing.

145
09:47.385 --> 09:48.225
Seriously.

146
09:49.505 --> 09:53.305
Hey, are the younger kids making content about us again?

147
09:53.385 --> 09:55.265
Everyone's suddenly talking about us.

148
09:56.425 --> 09:58.505
The advertising club again?

149
10:00.145 --> 10:01.745
What are they saying this time?

150
10:03.745 --> 10:05.265
Same old stuff.

151
10:05.345 --> 10:09.185
They're guessing what the Toxxxxin girls' lives are like.

152
10:09.745 --> 10:12.865
"They must have loads of celebrity friends."

153
10:12.945 --> 10:15.465
"They probably live super luxurious lives."

154
10:16.265 --> 10:18.265
"They must get to do whatever they want."

155
10:19.185 --> 10:20.465
Do whatever we want?

156
10:22.385 --> 10:23.225
Yeah, right.

157
10:23.305 --> 10:26.865
Things are probably about to get even tougher for Princess Aidao.

158
10:27.505 --> 10:30.305
Your dad's a minister now.

159
10:30.385 --> 10:35.145
I mean, sure. I'm absolutely happy.

160
10:37.265 --> 10:39.465
Doesn't that call for a toast?

161
10:39.545 --> 10:45.025
Congratulations to Colonel Sathit Laosathitphong.

162
10:45.105 --> 10:46.865
Cheers!

163
10:58.665 --> 11:02.625
Ugh, this sucks!

164
11:06.585 --> 11:08.345
What the hell are you doing?

165
11:20.505 --> 11:21.425
Guys.

166
11:22.945 --> 11:24.585
Thanks for everything.

167
11:24.665 --> 11:29.065
For sneaking out with me and keeping your accounts private,

168
11:29.145 --> 11:30.505
even though

169
11:32.225 --> 11:34.185
you're not being forced to like I am.

170
11:35.265 --> 11:36.385
Come on.

171
11:37.225 --> 11:39.425
We're not that different.

172
11:39.505 --> 11:40.345
Exactly.

173
11:40.945 --> 11:42.265
They don't have to force us.

174
11:42.345 --> 11:43.905
We don't really have a choice anyway.

175
11:48.345 --> 11:50.065
Damn, our lives are just…

176
11:51.505 --> 11:53.425
We seem to have everything…

177
11:55.625 --> 11:57.345
but we don't get a say in anything.

178
11:58.345 --> 11:59.985
We can't choose.

179
12:00.865 --> 12:02.225
We can't think for ourselves.

180
12:03.345 --> 12:04.745
We can't decide our own futures.

181
12:06.865 --> 12:08.705
We're not even

182
12:10.505 --> 12:12.105
allowed to dream.

183
12:16.025 --> 12:17.945
Enough with the drama.

184
12:19.985 --> 12:21.025
Yeah.

185
12:21.105 --> 12:23.265
Cheer up! Cheer up!

186
12:23.345 --> 12:24.465
Meimei!

187
12:25.825 --> 12:28.385
-It's not me who needs cheering up. -Who cares?

188
12:29.145 --> 12:30.185
I don't freaking know!

189
12:33.305 --> 12:34.265
Aidao?

190
12:35.865 --> 12:38.425
Don't worry about the dreams.

191
12:41.105 --> 12:42.665
You have every right to dream.

192
12:43.585 --> 12:45.585
Who can stop us from dreaming?

193
12:47.665 --> 12:48.505
Exactly.

194
12:48.585 --> 12:52.745
Our dreams are where we're most free.

195
12:53.545 --> 12:59.145
Speaking of this, Aidao, your dreams are the spiciest, aren't they?

196
12:59.225 --> 13:01.785
Those weird dreams you told us about,

197
13:01.865 --> 13:03.745
do you still have them?

198
13:07.505 --> 13:09.425
Well…

199
13:10.745 --> 13:12.465
I do, almost every day.

200
13:12.545 --> 13:13.985
Aww. Seriously?

201
13:14.065 --> 13:16.865
I told you. I've been saying it all along.

202
13:16.945 --> 13:18.505
It's a sign.

203
13:18.585 --> 13:21.785
Stop putting ideas in her head. You're always so dramatic.

204
13:21.865 --> 13:24.425
I'm not being dramatic. It really is romantic.

205
13:25.745 --> 13:26.585
Meimei!

206
13:27.305 --> 13:28.385
What?

207
13:31.065 --> 13:34.305
Yes, I've been having strange dreams for a long time.

208
13:39.185 --> 13:41.665
Even though I have them often,

209
13:41.745 --> 13:44.905
the details are hazy and hard to piece together.

210
13:47.785 --> 13:52.305
All I know is that there's always a girl I've never met.

211
13:54.065 --> 13:58.105
And every time, my heart races like it never has before.

212
13:59.825 --> 14:01.825
At first, I was excited.

213
14:02.505 --> 14:06.145
It felt like that girl gave me something to hope for.

214
14:07.945 --> 14:09.985
But as time went on,

215
14:10.065 --> 14:14.785
I began to feel it was too beautiful to be real.

216
14:17.505 --> 14:21.065
It was just a fantasy I'd created to fool myself.

217
14:24.385 --> 14:28.905
Even so, I couldn't help thinking,

218
14:29.665 --> 14:31.825
"I want to meet her so badly."

219
14:35.065 --> 14:36.545
-Shit! -Quick, help her!

220
14:36.625 --> 14:39.265
-Help her! -I'll jump in.

221
15:06.105 --> 15:07.785
Hey. Are you hurt?

222
15:08.465 --> 15:10.825
What the heck are you doing here?

223
15:12.065 --> 15:16.785
I was just walking around here, and I fell in.

224
15:16.865 --> 15:18.225
What do you mean, walking around?!

225
15:18.305 --> 15:20.145
Do you really expect us to believe that?

226
15:20.225 --> 15:21.905
Hey. Calm down.

227
15:22.705 --> 15:23.905
Let me talk to her.

228
15:32.945 --> 15:34.545
What happened?

229
15:38.585 --> 15:39.865
Please tell me.

230
16:37.465 --> 16:41.585
JUNJAI JANYAKUL

231
16:51.505 --> 16:54.145
Hey, you're sure nobody saw us?

232
16:54.225 --> 16:55.705
Yes. I checked.

233
16:57.825 --> 17:03.825
Okay, let's recap what just happened.

234
17:13.424 --> 17:14.345
I'm sorry.

235
17:29.665 --> 17:31.185
Why are you blushing?

236
17:36.025 --> 17:37.825
So, what were you doing here?

237
17:39.665 --> 17:41.865
I just wandered over here

238
17:42.905 --> 17:44.145
and fell in.

239
17:44.225 --> 17:46.105
Oh, please.

240
17:46.185 --> 17:47.865
We could tell you're lying even from Mars.

241
17:47.945 --> 17:49.065
It's true.

242
17:49.145 --> 17:50.785
And you don't need to worry.

243
17:50.865 --> 17:52.665
I'm completely fine. I should get going.

244
17:52.745 --> 17:54.305
Bye. Thank you.

245
18:00.705 --> 18:01.545
That was bad.

246
18:01.625 --> 18:02.825
It really was.

247
18:04.065 --> 18:06.305
And when we pulled her out again,

248
18:06.385 --> 18:08.425
she just burst into tears.

249
18:09.145 --> 18:12.745
After that, she wouldn't say another word.

250
18:12.825 --> 18:14.265
It was so weird.

251
18:16.945 --> 18:18.905
At least she let us take her home.

252
18:20.505 --> 18:24.225
And luckily, she exchanged contact details with Aidao.

253
18:24.305 --> 18:26.345
Otherwise, I wouldn't be able to sleep tonight.

254
18:26.425 --> 18:27.425
Right?

255
18:27.505 --> 18:30.225
JUNJAI, WHENEVER YOU'RE READY TO TALK, LET ME KNOW.

256
18:30.305 --> 18:32.105
PHONE CALL, VIDEO CALL

257
18:32.185 --> 18:33.465
Hey.

258
18:33.545 --> 18:34.385
Huh?

259
18:35.665 --> 18:36.985
Yeah, exactly.

260
18:37.665 --> 18:39.025
So what do we do now?

261
18:39.105 --> 18:43.305
We don't even know who she is.

262
18:43.385 --> 18:44.785
I checked.

263
18:44.865 --> 18:46.625
Her name's Junjai Janyakul.

264
18:46.705 --> 18:47.785
Grade 11, Class 1.

265
18:47.865 --> 18:50.345
She's from Lampang. She just transferred here on a scholarship.

266
18:50.425 --> 18:52.465
That was fast. Classic Gale.

267
18:52.545 --> 18:56.145
Still, that doesn't tell us what she was doing there.

268
18:58.025 --> 18:59.145
But seriously…

269
19:00.945 --> 19:02.905
There aren't many possibilities, right?

270
19:06.625 --> 19:07.465
Guys.

271
19:08.785 --> 19:10.025
It's bothering me.

272
19:11.145 --> 19:14.225
Let's go to the Grade 11 building tomorrow.

273
19:15.545 --> 19:16.945
But let's keep it low-key.

274
19:18.105 --> 19:19.505
I don't want to draw attention.

275
19:20.345 --> 19:24.025
Won't we draw attention just by showing up?

276
19:27.385 --> 19:29.345
GUYS!!!! THE TOXXXXIN GIRLS ARE AT THE GRADE 11 BUILDING!

277
19:30.185 --> 19:31.425
Have you seen this girl?

278
19:32.025 --> 19:33.105
Gosh!

279
19:34.025 --> 19:35.385
I'M DYING! #TOXXXXIN

280
19:35.465 --> 19:37.025
She's upstairs.

281
19:37.105 --> 19:38.505
-#TOXXXXIN -MY HEART CAN'T TAKE THIS.

282
19:38.585 --> 19:40.025
THEY'RE SO FREAKING GORGEOUS IN PERSON.

283
19:42.105 --> 19:43.985
ARE THEY HERE LOOKING FOR SOMEONE?

284
19:44.065 --> 19:45.865
-WHO'S THE LUCKY ONE? -OR DID SOMEONE PISS THEM OFF?

285
19:46.785 --> 19:48.745
-I WISH IT WERE ME. -WE'RE ALL HAVING GAY PANIC!

286
19:52.145 --> 19:54.785
Oh, JJ?

287
19:55.465 --> 19:56.785
Of course, we know her.

288
19:56.865 --> 19:58.105
She's in our class.

289
19:58.185 --> 20:00.105
We're not close, though.

290
20:00.825 --> 20:02.345
Did she cause you any trouble?

291
20:02.425 --> 20:04.465
Oh, no. Nothing like that.

292
20:04.545 --> 20:06.825
Do you know who she's close to?

293
20:06.905 --> 20:09.145
No one, really.

294
20:10.425 --> 20:14.785
Wait. Did you just call her JJ?

295
20:14.865 --> 20:18.425
Yeah. JJ, as in "jing jok," a house gecko.

296
20:20.945 --> 20:22.585
Doesn't she look like one?

297
20:24.825 --> 20:27.065
But we didn't come up with it.

298
20:27.145 --> 20:28.465
Everyone in our class calls her that.

299
20:29.585 --> 20:33.185
Then can you tell me who came up with it?

300
20:37.025 --> 20:37.865
Hey.

301
20:44.185 --> 20:47.505
-What happened? -Oh, something just dropped, ma'am.

302
20:47.585 --> 20:49.145
Just dropped? That was so loud.

303
20:49.225 --> 20:50.705
Move aside. Let me take a look.

304
20:50.785 --> 20:52.825
-You really can't go in, ma'am. -Girls, I said move aside.

305
20:52.905 --> 20:55.025
It's really nothing. Really, ma'am.

306
20:55.105 --> 20:56.025
Ma'am.

307
20:56.105 --> 20:58.665
-Please don't go in. -Move aside.

308
20:58.745 --> 21:00.425
It's really nothing, ma'am.

309
